From 764f1731c5856e9bb5ada893480a3720cd097143 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:09:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a run the holder ends frees its Board
 lease while the outbox is stalled

On a primary board the Board frees a run's lease only when the pushed card row leaves `running`.
With a host's push loop down (laptop-1 2026-11-13, SchemaAhead) that row never left the outbox, so
a run that parked normally kept its lease and the Board's stale-lease reaper booked it as a crash at
expiry: t_01a1d05e8be13a6a got two `stale_lease=macbook` failures and tripped its retry breaker.
Claims and renewals still reached the Board as direct calls; only the release was lost.

Every run-ending transition the holder makes now queues the run in the new
`kanban_run_end_lease.note` inside its txn (schedule, block, review handoff and the timed/escalation
parks through `_end_or_synthesize_run`; complete, request_changes, continue, archive, descendant
reopen), and `write_txn` sends `sync.release_lease(task, run_uid)` after COMMIT, the way operator
reclaim does. Best effort: any error is logged and the lease expires on the server as before; the
transition never fails. Rollback drops the queue, and a run whose end did not commit is skipped.
Crash/timeout/reclaim accounting paths do not queue (they release with their own charged outcome).

Gated on a stalled outbox (a due pending row older than 120 s). Board `releaseTask` returns a card it
still sees `running` to `ready` (and drops a placement card's runs_on). On a healthy host a direct
release would usually beat the row push, leaving a parked or done card claimable elsewhere until the
push lands, while the pushed row already ends the lease there.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_run_end_lease.py): schedule, block, complete, review and continue
release that run's run_uid with the outbox stalled (fail on main); a failing release (client error or
any exception) leaves the park intact (fails on main); a draining outbox, a crash end and a
rolled-back end send no release.

Card: t_01a1d41ac87b214b
